    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c01330c8-9bdc-4d7b-b355-90630c559bae&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201206552029_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Physical Therapy",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-04-08\n\nLocation: Fort Wayne\n\nPosition:  Associate Professor of Physical Therapy Department:  Doctorate of Physical Therapy Campus:  Fort Wayne, IN Target Hire Date:  January 2026 Are you someone who is looking for a meaningful opportunity to shape the next generation of physical therapists while providing leadership within an academic program? Manchester University invites applications for a full-time, 12‑month, non‑tenure‑track Associate Professor of Physical Therapy to join the Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) Program on the Fort Wayne campus. This role offers a significant opportunity for an experienced faculty member to contribute to program growth, curricular excellence, and student success through teaching, scholarship, service, and clinical engagement. What You'll Do:  Deliver engaging, evidence-based instruction in assigned courses. Contribute to course and curriculum design, assessment, and continuous improvement. Lead or participate in scholarly activities, including research, presentations, and publications. Serve on faculty committees and participate in professional and community service. Maintain clinical competence through ongoing practice and licensure. What You'll Need:  Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) required; PhD, EdD, or DSc strongly preferred. Minimum six years of experience as core faculty in a CAPTE-accredited DPT program. Three years of post-licensure clinical experience in physical therapy. Active or eligible Indiana Physical Therapy license. Demonstrated excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. Commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration and inclusive excellence. Why Manchester University? At MU, we:  Inclusive, Values-Driven Culture – We respect every individual and foster integrity, compassion, and service. Work-Life Balance – Generous paid time off, holidays, and flexible scheduling. Competitive Pay & Benefits – Comprehensive health coverage, retirement contributions, and tuition remission. Professional Growth – Tuition-free classes, development opportunities, and scholarly engagement. Wellness & Perks – Free PERC membership, caregiver leave, and employee assistance programs.     For more\ninformation about the position, please review the job description attached to\nthis posting.   To apply , please select the \"Apply\" button to begin the application process.           Manchester\nUniversity is an equal opportunity employer, and we are committed to respecting\nthe infinite worth of every individual.  We encourage\nindividuals of all backgrounds to apply.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c01330c8-9bdc-4d7b-b355-90630c559bae&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201206546555_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-04-08\n\nLocation: Fort Wayne\n\nPosition: Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy Department:  Physical Therapy Campus:  Fort Wayne, IN Target Hire Date:  May 2026 Are you looking for a meaningful opportunity to shape the next generation of physical therapists? Manchester University invites applications for a full-time, 12‑month, non‑tenure‑track Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy to join our collaborative and growing Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) Program on the Fort Wayne campus. This position offers the chance to make a lasting impact through teaching, mentorship, scholarship, and service while contributing to the continued development of a mission-driven academic program. What You'll Do:  Teach and develop didactic and/or clinical courses within the DPT curriculum. Contribute to curriculum design, assessment, and program development. Mentor and advise students, fostering a culture of success. Engage in scholarly activities, including research and dissemination of findings. Provide service through faculty governance, professional organizations, and community engagement. Maintain professional effectiveness through clinical practice and continuing education. What You'll Need:  Earned Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) degree; a PhD, EdD, DSc, or equivalent is preferred. Eligibility for Indiana physical therapy licensure. 3 years of clinical experience preferred. Teaching experience in a CAPTE-accredited physical therapy program preferred. Evidence of scholarly activity and a commitment to research strongly preferred. Strong communication, collaboration, and leadership skills. Why Manchester University? At MU, we:  Inclusive, Values-Driven Culture – We respect every individual and foster integrity, compassion, and service. Work-Life Balance – Generous paid time off, holidays, and flexible scheduling. Competitive Pay & Benefits – Comprehensive health coverage, retirement contributions, and tuition remission. Professional Growth – Tuition-free classes, development opportunities, and scholarly engagement. Wellness & Perks – Free PERC membership, caregiver leave, and employee assistance programs.   For more\ninformation about the position, please review the job description attached to\nthis posting.   To apply , please select the \"Apply\" button to begin the application process and s ubmit a cover letter, curriculum vita/resume, teaching philosophy, and evidence of effective teaching.       Manchester\nUniversity is an equal opportunity employer, and we are committed to respecting\nthe infinite worth of every individual.  We encourage\nindividuals of all backgrounds to apply.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c01330c8-9bdc-4d7b-b355-90630c559bae&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201173003756_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Lecturer of Physical Therapy",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-02-03\n\nLocation: Fort Wayne\n\nPosition:  Lecturer of Physical Therapy Department:  Doctorate of Physical Therapy Campus:  Fort Wayne Target Hire Date:  May 2026 The Doctorate of Physical Therapy  Adjunct Lecturer  will teach assigned courses within the DPT curriculum—didactic and/or laboratory-based—and engage in activities that support program goals and student success. This position reports to the Program Director and works closely with faculty and staff to deliver an exceptional educational experience aligned with CAPTE standards. What You'll Do:  Teach assigned DPT courses, including classroom and/or lab sessions. Develop and update course materials to meet program learning outcomes. Provide timely feedback and assessment of student performance. Mentor and guide students in their academic and professional development. Participate in faculty collaboration and course meetings as appropriate. What You'll Need:  Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) required; advanced degree (PhD, EdD, DHSc) preferred. Current, unrestricted physical therapy license in the United States. Prior teaching or clinical education experience strongly preferred. Commitment to excellence in teaching, learning, and professional practice. Why Manchester University?  At MU, we:  Respect the infinite worth of every individual Foster a campus culture rooted in integrity, compassion, and service Support a healthy work-life balance with generous time off and flexible scheduling Offer competitive salary and comprehensive benefits Invest in faculty development and encourage scholarly engagement For more information about the position, please review the job description attached to this posting.   To apply , please select the \"Apply\" button to begin the application process and include  a cover letter and curriculum vita/resume.     Manchester University is an equal opportunity employer, and we are committed to respecting the infinite worth of every individual.  We encourage individuals of all backgrounds to apply.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c01330c8-9bdc-4d7b-b355-90630c559bae&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201309255513_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Operations Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\n\nLocation: Fort Wayne\n\nExperiential Education Operations Specialist Manchester University | Fort Wayne, Indiana Bring organization to work that shapes future healthcare professionals. Manchester University is seeking an Experiential Education Operations Specialist for our Fort Wayne campus. This is an excellent opportunity for a highly organized, detail-oriented professional who enjoys improving processes, coordinating complex schedules, and building positive relationships. In this role, you will help create the structure behind meaningful clinical and experiential learning opportunities for students in health professions, nursing, and pharmacy. You will work closely with students, faculty, preceptors, and clinical partners to keep rotations, agreements, records, evaluations, and operational processes moving forward accurately and efficiently. What You’ll Do As part of the Office of Experiential Education, you will: Coordinate required and elective student rotations and clinical placements. Maintain affiliation agreements with experiential and clinical education sites. Develop and maintain databases containing site, preceptor, affiliate faculty, and program requirement information. Track required documentation and help ensure records are complete and current. Build and improve workflows that support efficient Office of Experiential Education operations. Communicate with students and preceptors about schedules, changes, requirements, and next steps. Prepare reports and support program evaluations associated with accreditation standards. Help identify better ways to organize information, streamline processes, and support the students and partners who rely on the office. Who Will Thrive in This Role? You may be a strong fit if you: Take pride in accuracy, follow-through, and meeting deadlines. Enjoy organizing detailed information and coordinating multiple priorities. Look for ways to improve processes rather than simply maintain them. Communicate clearly and professionally with a wide range of people. Remain responsive and solution-focused when schedules or priorities change. Value teamwork and understand how dependable behind-the-scenes work contributes to student success. Can hold yourself and others accountable for completing required information and meeting established expectations. Want to work in a collaborative environment where your contributions are visible and valued. Qualifications A high school diploma and administrative or clerical experience are required. A bachelor’s degree is preferred. Candidates must be proficient in Microsoft Office, the ability to learn and navigate software systems, and possess strong written and verbal communication skills, careful attention to detail, the ability to manage multiple responsibilities, and a commitment to collaborative, team-based outcomes. The successful candidate must also be able to interact effectively and professionally with internal and external stakeholders and demonstrate a commitment to professional development and an inclusive environment for students, faculty, and staff. Schedule and Location This is a full-time position based at Manchester University’s Fort Wayne campus . The regular schedule is 8 a.m. to 5 p.m., Monday through Friday, with occasional additional hours or schedule changes. Why Manchester? Manchester offers the chance to do meaningful work in a small, independent university community where relationships matter. You will join colleagues who care about students, value collaboration, and recognize the importance of thoughtful, reliable work. Eligible employees receive a total rewards package that supports professional growth and life outside of work, including: Four week of paid time off annually Health and wellness benefits Retirement benefits Professional development opportunities Tuition remission opportunities for eligible employees and qualifying family members, subject to University policy and eligibility requirements Manchester’s tuition remission program provides eligible full-time employees, spouses, and qualifying children with tuition benefits under the terms of the University’s policy. If you are ready to bring your organizational strengths to work that supports students, faculty, and healthcare partners, we invite you to apply. Build strong processes. Support student success. Make your work matter at Manchester.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c01330c8-9bdc-4d7b-b355-90630c559bae&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201309199321_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Department Chair - Pharmacy Practice, Assoc/P",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\n\nLocation: Fort Wayne\n\nDepartment Chair of Pharmacy Practice Manchester University | Fort Wayne, Indiana Lead with purpose. Advocate for faculty. Help shape the future of pharmacy education. Manchester University invites applications for the position of Department Chair of Pharmacy Practice at our Fort Wayne campus. This is an opportunity for an accomplished pharmacy educator and collaborative leader to make a visible difference within a close-knit, mission-driven university community. We are looking for a leader who brings structure and clarity to complex work, follows through on commitments, and is comfortable holding others accountable with fairness and transparency. The successful candidate will be an organized and engaged faculty advocate who listens well, communicates openly, and builds collaboration around shared goals. The Opportunity The Department Chair leads the Pharmacy Practice Department in advancing the mission, vision, and goals of the department and College. The position combines academic leadership with teaching, scholarship, and service. Approximately 60 to 70 percent of the role is devoted to administration, with the remaining responsibilities distributed among teaching and scholarship. As Department Chair, you will: Build a healthy, accountable department culture that supports excellence in teaching, professional accomplishment and meaningful personal lives. Establish clear expectations, follow through on commitments, and help faculty and staff take ownership of shared priorities. Collaborate with program leadership to maintain full accreditation status with ACPE. Advocate for faculty while balancing individual needs with departmental and institutional goals. Lead departmental planning, priority setting, resource stewardship, and continuous improvement. Recruit, retain, mentor, coach, and develop faculty and staff. Strengthen collaboration across disciplines and build partnerships that support teaching, practice, scholarship, and service. Contribute to teaching, scholarship, student mentoring, and University service. Work collaboratively with other chairs and deans. What You Will Bring Qualified candidates will have: An earned terminal degree in a pharmacy (BPharm or PharmD), preferably from an ACPE-accredited college or school of pharmacy. Credentials supporting appointment at the rank of associate or full professor. An understanding of contemporary pharmacy education and practice. Strong organizational, communication, coaching, and relationship-building skills. The ability to set priorities, manage deadlines, make thoughtful decisions, and hold others accountable. A commitment to faculty collaboration, advocacy, professional development, and student success. A demonstrated commitment to fostering an inclusive environment for students, faculty, and staff. Prior leadership experience in an academic or practice environment, experience with personnel and budget management, and experience developing clinical practice sites are preferred.  Why Manchester? At Manchester, leadership is personal. You will work in a community where colleagues know one another, collaboration matters, and your work can have a direct and lasting impact. The Fort Wayne campus is located in the city’s medical district and supports Manchester’s graduate and professional healthcare programs. It offers advanced facilities, collaborative learning spaces, and access to regional healthcare networks.  Eligible employees receive a total rewards package designed to support their professional and personal well-being, including: Paid time off Health and wellness benefits Retirement benefits Professional growth and development opportunities Tuition remission for eligible employees and qualifying family members, subject to University policy and eligibility requirements Manchester’s tuition remission program may cover tuition costs at the University that remain after applicable scholarships and grants. The governing policy includes eligibility, program, enrollment, and other requirements.  If you are ready to lead with accountability, advocate for faculty, and contribute to a university where relationships and mission still matter, we invite you to consider Manchester University. Join us in Fort Wayne. Lead with purpose. Make a difference.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c01330c8-9bdc-4d7b-b355-90630c559bae&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201309267046_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Student Employment - Career Closet & Campus Pantry Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\n\nLocation: North Manchester\n\nAbout the Role: The Career Closet & Campus Pantry Assistant supports student access to professional clothing and essential resources by maintaining inventory, organizing donations, and providing excellent customer service to students and campus visitors. Qualifications: Must be enrolled in classes at Manchester University Must be Federal Work Study eligible Key Responsibilities: Manage Campus Pantry inventory, including stocking, restocking, and removing expired or damaged items. Organize, sort, and maintain Career Closet donations. Monitor and record temperatures of the pantry room, refrigerators, and freezers, and other required operational data. Welcome, assist, and provide information to students and visitors utilizing pantry and Career Closet services. Ensure both spaces remain clean, organized, and accessible. Assist with inventory tracking and reporting as needed. Maintain confidentiality regarding pantry clients, etc. Estimated Start Date: ASAP",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c01330c8-9bdc-4d7b-b355-90630c559bae&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201309544761_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Dean, School of Pharmacy",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\n\nLocation: Fort Wayne\n\nDean, School of Pharmacy Manchester University | Fort Wayne, Indiana Lead with vision. Build strong teams. Shape the future of pharmacy education. Manchester University is seeking a collaborative, accountable, and forward-thinking leader to serve as Dean of the School of Pharmacy at our Fort Wayne campus. This is an opportunity to lead a distinctive portfolio of programs while helping shape the future of health professions education at a small, mission-driven university. The Dean provides strategic, academic, and operational leadership for the School’s Doctor of Pharmacy, Master of Science in Pharmacogenomics, and Master of Science in Nutrition and Nutrigenomics programs, including related dual-degree and graduate certificate offerings.  The successful candidate will be an organized and transparent leader who follows through on commitments, holds themselves and others accountable, and creates an environment where faculty and staff can do their best work. We are looking for someone who advocates for faculty, encourages collaboration, communicates clearly, and can turn strategic priorities into meaningful action. Why This Leadership Opportunity? The Dean will have the opportunity to: Guide academic innovation across pharmacy, pharmacogenomics, nutrition, and nutrigenomics. Strengthen academic quality, accreditation readiness, and continuous improvement. Support faculty development, scholarship, and professional engagement. Build partnerships with healthcare systems, industry, universities, alumni, and community organizations. Develop enrollment pathways and new academic offerings that respond to workforce needs. Help create a collaborative, accountable culture centered on students, faculty success, and academic excellence. Co-lead the College of Health Professions, Nursing & Pharmacy alongside the Dean of the School of Health Professions and Nursing.  What You’ll Do As Dean, you will: Provide strategic direction for the School and align its goals with University and college priorities. Lead and support department chairs, program directors, faculty, and staff in curriculum development, assessment, accreditation, and continuous improvement. Lead school operations, budget planning, personnel decisions, policy development, and resource allocation. Promote sustainable enrollment growth and sound fiscal stewardship. Champion faculty advocacy, professional development, mentoring, scholarship, and research collaboration. Foster open communication, shared accountability, inclusive leadership, and effective collaboration. Strengthen student recruitment, retention, licensure readiness, career preparation, and professional development. Cultivate relationships with alumni, advisory boards, healthcare organizations, industry partners, professional associations, and community stakeholders. Support fundraising and alumni engagement in partnership with University Advancement and Alumni Relations. Represent the School in University governance and in external academic, regulatory, and professional settings.  What We’re Looking For The successful candidate will bring: A terminal degree in pharmacy. Significant experience with accreditation, curriculum oversight, academic assessment, and program development. Familiarity with HLC, ACPE, and/or ACEND accreditation standards. Demonstrated academic or administrative leadership experience. Strong organizational, supervisory, budgetary, and team-building skills. A record of building productive relationships with faculty, staff, students, trustees, community partners, and professional organizations. The ability to make informed decisions, communicate expectations, and promote accountability. A collaborative leadership style that values faculty expertise, shared governance, and transparent communication. A commitment to student success, inclusive excellence, innovation, and Manchester University’s mission. Excellent written and verbal communication skills and the ability to represent the University with professionalism and integrity. Candidates whose leadership experience has been developed through academic administration, pharmacy education, healthcare, industry, research, accreditation, or related settings are encouraged to apply. Why Manchester University? At Manchester, leadership is personal. As a small, independent university, we offer the opportunity to know the people behind the programs, build meaningful relationships, and see the impact of your work. The University offers a comprehensive total rewards package that includes: Over four weeks of paid time off and University holidays Tuition benefits for employees and eligible family members Medical, dental, and vision coverage Retirement benefits Professional development opportunities A collaborative, mission-driven university community The opportunity to live and work in Fort Wayne, a growing community with the amenities of a larger city and the accessibility of the Midwest This is a full-time, 12-month, exempt staff position. The role is based in Fort Wayne and includes occasional travel and periodic evening and weekend responsibilities.  Make Your Next Leadership Chapter Matter If you are an academic leader who believes that accountability and advocacy belong together, who can bring structure to complex work, and who wants to help faculty, staff, and students thrive, we invite you to consider joining Manchester University as our next Dean of the School of Pharmacy . Manchester University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants who require a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process are encouraged to contact Human Resources.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c01330c8-9bdc-4d7b-b355-90630c559bae&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201310025935_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Lecturer of Pharmacogenomics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-17\n\nPosition: Adjunct Faculty in Biostatistics Department: Pharmaceutical and Graduate Life Sciences Campus: Remote Target Teaching Date:  May 2027 Compensation for this position is $1,500.00 per load hour.  Position Overview: This is a part-time teaching position adjunct faculty position with additional responsibilities related to the academic program for the Summer semester of 2027. It reports through the department chair to the Dean of the College of Pharmacy. Essential Job Functions Deliver a 3-credit hour 500-level Biostatistics course  Asynchronous distance pathway delivery Ensure all materials are posted 2 weeks in advance of delivery Maintain regular interactions with enrolled students Report final grades to the registrar Meeting assigned classes at the scheduled locations, as needed Holding regular office hours Administering examinations and assessing student learning Working in a professional, collegial and team-oriented manner with the University community Maintaining compliance with policies and procedures in the Faculty Manual  Maintaining office hours, as appropriate  Secondary Job functions Supporting students’ personal and professional development  Designing new courses, as appropriate Academic advising  Qualifications Ph.D. in Biostatistics or a related field, or an advanced degree accompanied by documented subject-matter expertise and/or appropriate professional certification Knowledge and experience sufficient to enable the candidate to effectively teach courses as assigned in specified department Effective presentation skills Effective organizational and administrative skills Ability to deliver course content and to assist students in understanding course content Ability to evaluate student writing and to provide effective feedback Ability to communicate effectively orally and in writing with students, faculty, staff, and administrators Ability to adapt to changing teaching and learning environments and content-delivery methods Ability to work cooperatively with colleagues, in the best interests of the students Ability to prioritize responsibilities, meet deadlines, and respond to students’ legitimate needs in a timely manner Ability and willingness to work with students of all skill levels and academic backgrounds Ability and willingness to perform clerical work for oneself, as necessary Proficient in spoken and written English Basic computer proficiency in word processing, spreadsheet, e-mail and internet use Work Schedule: determined by hire",
      "department": ""
    }
  },
